{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is centered with generous negative space, captured from a 3/4 overhead angle to clearly display the volume of the dish. A shallow depth of field keeps the foreground plate sharp while the background elements softly blur. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the glistening beef and melted feta. The setting features a rustic, aged oak wood table with faint signs of use. The dish is served on two simple, matte-white ceramic plates; the foreground plate holds two large, roasted portobello mushroom caps filled with a savory mixture of browned, crumbled extra-lean beef, wilted vibrant green baby spinach, and small pieces of diced tomato. The filling is topped with a rustic scattering of white, crumbly feta cheese. Beside the mushrooms, a neat mound of fluffy, light-tan cooked quinoa sits on the plate. A tarnished silver fork rests casually on the linen tablecloth beside the plates. A few stray quinoa grains and a single fresh spinach leaf are scattered naturally on the wood surface near the plate, suggesting a lived-in kitchen. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a home-cooked meal, warm and inviting. Small imperfections like a tiny smear of sauce on the rim and uneven browning on the mushrooms ensure authenticity. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
}
